00:22:59.110 --> 00:23:00.590
So when you think about
kind of a big picture

00:23:00.590 --> 00:23:02.570
of how people are allocated across space

00:23:02.570 --> 00:23:04.260
and urban economists
are thinking about this

00:23:04.260 --> 00:23:06.610
in terms of the returns to scale

00:23:06.610 --> 00:23:09.790
in that you get from positive
kind of agglomeration

00:23:11.307 --> 00:23:13.550
in, versus congestion costs
if you think about traffic

00:23:13.550 --> 00:23:15.400
but especially rent.

00:23:15.400 --> 00:23:17.650
And so if we think about kind
of there's one existing city

00:23:17.650 --> 00:23:20.100
and a wave of forced migrants arrive,

00:23:20.100 --> 00:23:23.540
if we just kind of let
the market allocate this

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:26.980
on kind of the margin,
then households can choose

00:23:26.980 --> 00:23:28.370
either the city or the desert

00:23:28.370 --> 00:23:30.660
based on their own kind of private returns

00:23:30.660 --> 00:23:33.270
and their, they kind of feel benefit

00:23:33.270 --> 00:23:35.920
to always kind of locating in the city.

00:23:35.920 --> 00:23:39.280
But at some point there might
be more negative externalities

00:23:39.280 --> 00:23:41.300
for the marginal person coming in,

00:23:41.300 --> 00:23:44.633
than the, than the positive social costs.

00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:47.620
And so if we think

00:23:47.620 --> 00:23:50.930
about then they would allocate
themselves all into one city

00:23:50.930 --> 00:23:53.840
and this total welfare would be positive

00:23:53.840 --> 00:23:56.600
but would eventually start to decline

00:23:56.600 --> 00:23:57.860
as urban economists have noted

00:23:57.860 --> 00:24:01.580
that some cities seem to be like too large

00:24:01.580 --> 00:24:04.253
relative to the, the costs and benefits.

00:24:05.250 --> 00:24:07.640
If we think about a
social planner instead,

00:24:07.640 --> 00:24:09.370
that they could choose these city sizes

00:24:09.370 --> 00:24:12.580
based on the total social
welfare, you could have,

00:24:12.580 --> 00:24:15.060
you could divide this group into two

00:24:15.060 --> 00:24:18.930
and doubled the social benefit
where, where it's positive

00:24:18.930 --> 00:24:21.100
and at some point with a
large enough population,

00:24:21.100 --> 00:24:26.100
you have the total social
welfare exceeds, with two cities,

00:24:26.470 --> 00:24:29.530
exceeds the kind of like
marginal everyone deciding this

00:24:29.530 --> 00:24:31.683
for themselves of, of one city.

00:24:32.710 --> 00:24:35.050
And so one potential
way to think about this

00:24:35.050 --> 00:24:37.920
is camps is acting as a
coordinating mechanism

00:24:37.920 --> 00:24:42.920
for new, new arrivals
to, to locate around.

00:24:46.930 --> 00:24:50.020
So I think many people are
familiar with the context,

